{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content docs/log.d/2026-10-07-wi841-retro-owner-rulings.md | Select-String -Pattern '\"'^##|''^###|held|state|trunk|ruling 5'\"' -Context 0,8; Get-Content project-trajectory/scripts/held_status.py | Select-Object -Skip 355 -First 245; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"\r\n> ## 2026-10-07 — Owner rulings from the WI-841 retrospective\r\n  \r\n  A retrospective of the WI-841 lane\r\n  ([spec](../archive/work/complete/WI-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane.md)) asked\r\n  why it took as long as it did. Two causes were found:\r\n  - Code and spine work alternated, so every code fix re-opened rows and owed\r\n    another sitting.\r\n  - The coordinator's hand path has become a second copy of the loop's cycle.\r\n    It writes its own prompts, runs no plan, critique or findings gate, and its\r\n>      parent states verified.\r\n>    - In a lane touching a held rung: the set splits at the dial.\r\n     A spine is decomposed consistently in all three.\r\n  4. **A child is approved only after its parent.** No check enforces this yet.\r\n     LLR-281 and TC-291 are Approved under SR-224, which is still `Drafted`.\r\n> 5. **Held-rung rows are protected by state alone:** the live registry, the\r\n>    snapshot and the dial. The rule judges what lands from a lane. A held row\r\n     whose snapshot moved to match changed text is refused unless the change was\r\n>    CLARITY, recorded in the verdict. A direct trunk approval by the owner or an\r\n     authorized approver is not judged.\r\n  6. **The approval act is kit-wide in the lane.** An independent adjudicator\r\n>    may take the act in the authoring lane. This supersedes the trunk-side\r\n     clause of the 2026-09-01 ruling. PROCESS.md and the merge slot do not say\r\n     so yet: one row changes both, carrying the S11 plan's unbuilt approval-act\r\n     rung change, so the doc never runs ahead of the check.\r\n  7. **The two-hour Codex relaxation stands.** After two hours unavailable, a\r\n     fresh independent Opus reviewer may review, recorded as a same-family\r\n     relaxation.\r\n> 8. **The verdict rollup stays generated on trunk.** A lane never commits it.\r\n  9. **The coordinator's procedure moves into one this-repo skill,**\r\n>    `coordinator-cycle`. Handoffs go back to holding state only.\r\n  10. **One authoring model for spine text.** Terra, or another declared author\r\n      role, does the first authoring pass, and the adjudicator passes judgement.\r\n      The adjudicator never drafts the text it judges. This re-scopes WI-812,\r\n      which followed the design's \"the adjudicator drafts\" (OI-101 Q1's drafting\r\n      half; README changes 4 and 14, now annotated as superseded).\r\n  \r\n  Four further questions surfaced by the queue reconciliation are filed as open\r\n  items, each cited by the row that waits on it:\r\n> - OI-109, the rollup when the trunk step runs lane-side (WI-800, WI-807);\r\n  - OI-110, where the token-file dial lives (WI-846);\r\n  - OI-111, WI-811's final-review family rule.\r\n  \r\n  Already landed: `bec70dc5` corrects PROCESS.md §4's description of the dial,\r\n  which still called it a 0–4 ordinal, to the `DevStg-*` rung it has been since\r\n  OI-21 shape (ii).\r\n  \r\n  Rows for the next coordinator session to file, each with its own lane:\r\n> - ruling 5: the state-based held-rung check, retiring the trailer-armed\r\n>   `held-status` arm and the act-ledger CLARITY arm;\r\n  - the coordinator renders its review and critique briefs from the kit\r\n    templates, with the untracked coordinator tools brought into the repo;\r\n  - `plan_coverage --findings` wired into rework, on both the loop and the\r\n    coordinator path;\r\n  - the adjudication briefs compose `spine-authoring`'s tier questions at\r\n    render time;\r\n  - the verdict rollup reads the coordinator's review files.\r\n  \r\n>   older staleness fixes (WI-827, landed on trunk by the owner's act).\r\n  - **OI-107 (b):** a decisions record is named by its work item; a decision tied\r\n    to no work item takes the next number above the highest such decision. A\r\n    decision watermark is the deferred cleaner option (WI-832).\r\n  - **OI-108:** no second relaxation. The coordinator's relaxation is the kit's\r\n    one alternative-agent rule, the reviewer ladder that ends same-family and\r\n    records it, in whatever form later rows give it (WI-801, cited by WI-811).\r\n> - **OI-109 (a):** under the station authority, the rollup the lane-side trunk\r\n>   step writes is trunk's (WI-800, WI-807).\r\n  - **OI-111 (a):** the final reviewer's family is a preference, never an\r\n    author's session, yielding only by the alternative-agent rule (WI-811).\r\n  \r\n  OI-110 stays pending. The owner prefers (b), an environment variable naming\r\n> the token file, and asked how the path is held today: it is in no tracked\r\n  file, only in the coordinator's local agent memory outside the repository.\r\n  \r\n  At the owner's direction the retrospective's rows were then filed as WI-848 to\r\n  WI-854 (P1 to P7, with P8 folded into WI-852). The queued rows that waited on\r\n  their ids were updated to cite them, and one consolidation sitting was run\r\n  with them in the queue.\r\n  \r\n  The session took the coordinator lease only after the design work, and the\r\ndef registry_held(dial, registry):\r\n    \"\"\"Does `dial` hold the rung `registry`'s status cells are approved into?\r\n    A registry the rung map does not name is held whatever the dial says.\r\n\r\n    Implements: SR-208, LLR-246\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    rung = _kitauthority.rung_for(registry)\r\n    return rung is None or _kitauthority.holds_under(dial, rung)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _approves(row):\r\n    return row is not None and _kitspine.claims_approval(row)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _copy_claim(registry, id_col, rid, copy_after, copy_before):\r\n    \"\"\"Is row `rid`'s copy movement a (b) claim: the copy claims approval and\r\n    the row entered it, or moved in an approved cell or in `Status`; or the\r\n    copy held it approved and holds it no more.\"\"\"\r\n    now, was = copy_after.get(rid), copy_before.get(rid)\r\n    if now is None:\r\n        return _approves(was)\r\n    if not _approves(now):\r\n        return False\r\n    if was is None or (now.get(\"Status\") or \"\") != (was.get(\"Status\") or \"\"):\r\n        return True\r\n    cells = acceptance_record.split_changed_cells(registry, id_col, was, now)\r\n    return bool(cells[\"approved\"])\r\n\r\n\r\ndef held_claims(after, before, held):\r\n    \"\"\"`{(row id, registry, id column): \"a\" | \"b\"}`: every approval claim one\r\n    side `after` makes against one side `before`, on a registry `held(registry)`\r\n    holds. Each side maps `(registry, id column)` to `(live rows, copy rows)`.\r\n    (a) is a live move into approval, a row born approved included; (b) a copy\r\n    movement `_copy_claim` reads as one. Example `-000` rows are skipped.\r\n\r\n    Implements: SR-208, LLR-246\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    out = {}\r\n    for key in set(after) | set(before):\r\n        registry, id_col = key\r\n        if not held(registry):\r\n            continue\r\n        live_a, copy_a = after.get(key, ({}, {}))\r\n        live_b, copy_b = before.get(key, ({}, {}))\r\n        for rid in set(live_a) | set(copy_a) | set(copy_b):\r\n            if str(rid).endswith(\"-000\"):\r\n                continue\r\n            if _approves(live_a.get(rid)) and not _approves(live_b.get(rid)):\r\n                out[(rid, registry, id_col)] = \"a\"\r\n            elif _copy_claim(registry, id_col, rid, copy_a, copy_b):\r\n                out[(rid, registry, id_col)] = \"b\"\r\n    return out\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _side(root, prefix):\r\n    \"\"\"`({(registry, id column): (live rows, copy rows)}, failures)` of every\r\n    held tier in the tree `prefix`, each read from the first carrier the tree\r\n    lists (an absent one is no rows); one `\"<path> cannot be read\"` or\r\n    `\"<path> does not parse\"` failure per carrier that fails.\"\"\"\r\n    side, failures = {}, []\r\n    for rel, col in HELD_TIERS:\r\n        pair = []\r\n        for under in (\"\", _RECORD):\r\n            rows = {}\r\n            reads = acceptance_record._tier_reads(root, prefix, rel, col, under)\r\n            for path, found, failure in reads:\r\n                if failure:\r\n                    failures.append(\"{} {}\".format(path, failure))\r\n                rows = found or {}\r\n                break\r\n            pair.append(rows)\r\n        side[(rel, col)] = tuple(pair)\r\n    return side, failures\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _bound_clarity(root, rev, rid, digest):\r\n    \"\"\"True when an accepted amendment verdict committed in the tree `rev`\r\n    (None: the index) rules row `rid` CLARITY and its binding records `digest`\r\n    for it; False when none does; None when git cannot search the tree. The\r\n    candidates are the bindings under `docs/reviews/` that name the row.\"\"\"\r\n    found = _kitgit.grep_files(root, rev, rid + \"=\", _REVIEWS)\r\n    if found is None:\r\n        return None\r\n    for path in found:\r\n        if not path.endswith(_kitsitting.REQUESTED_SUFFIX):\r\n            continue\r\n        verdict = path[: -len(_kitsitting.REQUESTED_SUFFIX)]\r\n        part = (_kitsitting.accepted_at(root, rev, verdict) or {}).get(\"amendment\")\r\n        if not part or part[3].get(rid) != \"CLARITY\":\r\n            continue\r\n        identities, _why = _kitsitting.accepted_identities(root, rev, verdict)\r\n        if identities and identities.get(rid) == digest:\r\n            return True\r\n    return False\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _excepted(root, head, key, after, befores):\r\n    \"\"\"`(True, None)` when the (b) claim `key` is a CLARITY re-attestation\r\n    bound to the row's text at `head`; `(False, None)` when it is not; and\r\n    `(False, line)` when git cannot search for its verdict.\"\"\"\r\n    rid, registry, id_col = key\r\n    live, copy = after[(registry, id_col)]\r\n    row = live.get(rid)\r\n    if not _approves(row) or copy.get(rid) != row:\r\n        return False, None\r\n    for before in befores:\r\n        was = before.get((registry, id_col), ({}, {}))[0].get(rid)\r\n        if not _approves(was) or (was.get(\"Status\") or \"\") != row.get(\"Status\"):\r\n            return False, None\r\n    digest = acceptance_record.approved_text_digest(registry, id_col, row)\r\n    bound = _bound_clarity(root, head, rid, digest)\r\n    if bound is None:\r\n        return False, \"git cannot search {} for the verdict binding {}\".format(\r\n            _REVIEWS, rid\r\n        )\r\n    return bound, None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _touched(root, bases, head):\r\n    \"\"\"`(touched, line)`: whether the tree `head` (None: the index) changes a\r\n    held carrier against any of `bases`, or a line when git cannot list it.\"\"\"\r\n    side = [head] if head else [\"--cached\"]\r\n    touched = False\r\n    for base in bases:\r\n        args = [\"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"--no-renames\", base, *side, \"--\"]\r\n        names = _kitgit.git_paths(root, args + list(HELD_PATHS))\r\n        if names is None:\r\n            return False, \"git cannot list what it changes against {}\".format(base[:10])\r\n        touched = touched or bool(names)\r\n    return touched, None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _claims_against(root, bases, head, dial):\r\n    \"\"\"`(claims, after, befores, lines)`: the held claims the tree `head`\r\n    (None: the index) makes against EVERY base, its own side, each base's\r\n    side, and the refusal lines for a list git cannot produce or a carrier of\r\n    the head side that cannot be read or does not parse. A base side that\r\n    fails reads as no rows, so every approval-claiming row of the head side\r\n    counts as a claim.\"\"\"\r\n    touched, line = _touched(root, bases, head)\r\n    if line or not touched:\r\n        return {}, {}, [], [line] if line else []\r\n    after, failures = _side(root, \":\" if head is None else head + \":\")\r\n    if failures:\r\n        return (\r\n            {},\r\n            after,\r\n            [],\r\n            [f + \", so its held approval claims are unknown\" for f in failures],\r\n        )\r\n    claims, befores = _every_base(root, bases, after, dial)\r\n    return claims, after, befores, []\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _every_base(root, bases, after, dial):\r\n    \"\"\"`(claims, befores)`: the held claims the side `after` makes against\r\n    every base, kept only when made against each, and each base's side; a\r\n    base side that fails reads as no rows.\"\"\"\r\n    held = functools.partial(registry_held, dial)\r\n    claims, befores = None, []\r\n    for base in bases:\r\n        before, failed = _side(root, base + \":\")\r\n        before = {} if failed else before\r\n        befores.append(before)\r\n        found = held_claims(after, before, held)\r\n        claims = (\r\n            found if claims is None else {k: v for k, v in claims.items() if k in found}\r\n        )\r\n    return claims or {}, befores\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _claim_line(key, kind, dial):\r\n    rid, registry, _id_col = key\r\n    rung = _kitauthority.rung_for(registry) or \"unmapped, so held\"\r\n    what = (\r\n        \"its Status moved into approval\"\r\n        if kind == \"a\"\r\n        else \"its approval record copy moved\"\r\n    )\r\n    return \"{} {} claims approval on a held rung ({}; human_approval_through = {}): {}\".format(\r\n        spine_carrier.stem(registry).rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1], rid, rung, dial, what\r\n    )\r\n\r\n\r\ndef held_approval_lines(root, bases, head, dial):\r\n    \"\"\"THE LANE RULE over one tree: the refusal lines for every held approval\r\n    claim the tree `head` (None: the index) makes against every tree of\r\n    `bases`, judged under `dial`, each naming the tree, the row, its rung and\r\n    the dial and carrying `HELD_REMEDY`, a (b) claim the one exception admits\r\n    excepted; or one line per carrier that cannot be read or does not parse,\r\n    naming it. `[]` when the tree touches no held carrier.\r\n\r\n    Implements: SR-208, LLR-246\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    tree = \"the index\" if head is None else \"commit \" + head[:10]\r\n    claims, after, befores, lines = _claims_against(root, bases, head, dial)\r\n    for key, kind in sorted(claims.items()):\r\n        excepted, line = (False, None)\r\n        if kind == \"b\":\r\n            excepted, line = _excepted(root, head, key, after, befores)\r\n        if not excepted:\r\n            lines.append(\r\n                line or \"{} - {}\".format(_claim_line(key, kind, dial), HELD_REMEDY)\r\n            )\r\n    return [\"{}: {}\".format(tree, line) for line in lines]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef commit_held_approval_lines(root, rev):\r\n    \"\"\"The lane rule for one lane commit, the rider the merge slot's\r\n    lane-commit walk runs: `held_approval_lines` against every parent of its\r\n    commit object (`acceptance_record._commit_parents`, so an unreadable\r\n    parent is a line), under the dial committed at HEAD, which is trunk at\r\n    the slot and at a squash landing. A root commit is not judged.\r\n\r\n    Implements: SR-208, LLR-246\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    parents, unread = acceptance_record._commit_parents(\r\n        root, rev, \"it makes a held approval claim\"\r\n    )\r\n    if unread or not parents:\r\n        return unread\r\n    return held_approval_lines(root, parents, rev, _kitauthority.dial_at(root, \"HEAD\"))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _spine_status_moves(root, base, head, registries):\r\n    \"\"\"Every `Status` move of the spine rows in `registries` between `base`\r\n    and `head` (None: the index), in `staged_status_moves`' shape: the one\r\n    spine status walk the history check and the marker arm share.\r\n\r\n    Implements: SR-208, SR-210, LLR-246, LLR-249\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    moves = []\r\n    for registry, _id_col, before, after, _csv in acceptance_record._spine_row_sides(\r\n        root, base, head, registries\r\n    ):\r\n        for rid in sorted(set(before) | set(after)):\r\n            was = ((before.get(rid) or {}).get(\"Status\") or \"\").strip()\r\n            now = ((after.get(rid) or {}).get(\"Status\") or \"\").strip()\r\n            if was != now:\r\n                moves.append(\r\n                    {\"registry\": registry, \"id\": rid, \"before\": was, \"after\": now}\r\n                )\r\n    return moves\r\n\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"rg -n 'WI-851|LLR-246|state' docs/work/deferred/WI-800-session-store-and-usage-ledger.md docs/work/deferred/WI-809-in-lane-sitting.md; Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 3237 -First 12; Get-Content project-trajectory/scripts/held_status.py | Select-Object -Skip 600 -First 66; git diff --check 31b8ed9414fbf452c6688c7b0ab9bde10bb71651...a02a18284c87ed3fe641e916f547de182a751920 -- . ':(exclude)docs/iteration' ':(exclude)docs/reviews' ':(exclude)docs/decisions' ':(exclude)docs/plans/*/critique-*' ':(exclude)docs/log.md' ':(exclude)docs/log.d' ':(exclude)PROJECT_STATE.html' ':(exclude)docs/open-items.html' ':(exclude)docs/stage'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"rg -n 'WI-851|LLR-246|state' docs/work/deferred/WI-800-session-store-and-usage-ledger.md docs/work/deferred/WI-809-in-lane-sitting.md; Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 3237 -First 12; Get-Content project-trajectory/scripts/held_status.py | Select-Object -Skip 600 -First 66; git diff --check 31b8ed9414fbf452c6688c7b0ab9bde10bb71651...a02a18284c87ed3fe641e916f547de182a751920 -- . ':(exclude)docs/iteration' ':(exclude)docs/reviews' ':(exclude)docs/decisions' ':(exclude)docs/plans/*/critique-*' ':(exclude)docs/log.md' ':(exclude)docs/log.d' ':(exclude)PROJECT_STATE.html' ':(exclude)docs/open-items.html' ':(exclude)docs/stage'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/work/deferred/WI-809-in-lane-sitting.md:7:needs = [\"WI-808\", \"WI-806\", \"WI-802\", \"WI-849\", \"WI-850\", \"WI-851\", \"WI-857\"]\ndocs/work/deferred/WI-809-in-lane-sitting.md:28:WI-851's state rule; the design's ch.4 row keeping `_held_status_refusal`\ndocs/work/deferred/WI-809-in-lane-sitting.md:29:\"unchanged\" is superseded by WI-851. WI-791's contract is complete, so it is\ndocs/work/deferred/WI-809-in-lane-sitting.md:43:- Held-rung rows in an in-lane act are judged by WI-851's state-based check,\ndocs/work/deferred/WI-800-session-store-and-usage-ledger.md:7:needs = [\"WI-798\", \"WI-799\", \"OI-109\", \"WI-851\", \"WI-847\", \"WI-858\", \"WI-960\"]\ndocs/work/deferred/WI-800-session-store-and-usage-ledger.md:51:  shared with WI-802; LLR-137 shared with WI-807; LLR-246 shared with WI-807 and\ndocs/work/deferred/WI-800-session-store-and-usage-ledger.md:52:  WI-810; a new LLR for the ledger with a TC verifying each arm it states) is\ndocs/work/deferred/WI-800-session-store-and-usage-ledger.md:55:- Its LLR-246 amendment follows WI-851's state rule; it adds no per-writer\n[design.LLR-302]\r\nsr_refs = [\"SR-140\"]\r\ntitle = \"Approval-record text is committed before the approval act\"\r\nmodule = \"project-trajectory/scripts/acceptance_record.py;project-trajectory/scripts/check.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/text_then_act.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py\"\r\ncode_symbol = \"_commit_parents/_text_changes/_row_text_moves/text_then_act_lines/commit_text_then_act_lines/lane_commit_walk/squash_walk/_squash_lines/staged_text_then_act_lines/_text_then_act_refusal/_with_text_then_act_remedy/_text_then_act_mode/_each_lane_commit/squash_commits\"\r\ndetail = \"text_then_act_lines judges a tree that writes under the approval record against its parent trees and reports every approval-act row in it whose cell other than Status changed, a traced cell included, or which was added or removed; a tree that writes no record is not judged. A record path, cell or row counts only when it differs from every parent, so a merge, a refresh merge included, reports only what neither parent carried, and a diff git cannot read is reported rather than skipped. commit_text_then_act_lines judges one commit against every parent its commit object names; a parent the repository cannot read is reported by name, and a root commit has no preceding text and passes. staged_text_then_act_lines judges the index against HEAD, and against MERGE_HEAD as well while a merge is in progress; before the first commit nothing is judged. While git's SQUASH_MSG names a squashed tip, the index is exempt only when HEAD is an ancestor of that tip and the approval-act registries and record in the index are byte-equal to the tip's; then each commit HEAD..tip is judged against its parents and the index is not. Otherwise the index is judged like any commit, and a refusal tells the operator to rebase the lane onto trunk first. Git keeps no other squash state, so a SQUASH_MSG that an abandoned squash left behind grants the same exemption, on the same conditions, to at most the next commit, since git deletes the message when that commit is made. The pre-commit step refuses any reported line. The merge slot judges each lane commit not yet on trunk and refuses the lane, naming a reported commit, so a commit made without the hook cannot land the mixed change.\"\r\nrationale = \"The record names the author of the commit that writes the copy as the acting reviewer of the text the copy carries. That attribution holds only when the text was committed, and readable for review, before that commit: text riding the act has no commit of its own, so who wrote it and who accepted it cannot be told apart by query. Checking only at the hook would leave a commit made without it unguarded, and checking only at the landing would leave direct commits unguarded, so one comparison over two trees serves both. A merge is judged by what neither parent carried because a refresh that brings in trunk's text commit and act commit together is its parents' work, not the lane's own mixed act. A squash landing is admitted on the commits it folds in rather than on trust, because a hand landing never meets the merge slot. The exemption is verified on content rather than on the message: the spine and record a commit it admits stages are a lane tip's own, byte for byte, and every commit HEAD..tip was judged, so it could equally have landed as that tip's squash; telling a hand-made commit from the squash would need a provenance marker, which enforcing at the commit against its parents rules out.\"\r\ntest_refs = \"TC-173\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-006\"\r\nphase = 6\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _named(paths):\r\n    return None if paths is None else {str(p).replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\").strip() for p in paths}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _own_moves(root, bases, head, paths):\r\n    \"\"\"The status moves `head` makes against every base, off-spine and on the\r\n    marker arm's spine tiers, narrowed to `paths` when given: each move of the\r\n    first base whose row also moved against every other base.\"\"\"\r\n    named, own = _named(paths), None\r\n    for base in bases:\r\n        moves = staged_status_moves(root, base, head, paths)\r\n        spine = _spine_status_moves(root, base, head, MARKED_SPINE)\r\n        moves += [m for m in spine if named is None or m[\"registry\"] in named]\r\n        keys = {(m[\"registry\"], m[\"id\"]) for m in moves}\r\n        own = (\r\n            moves\r\n            if own is None\r\n            else [m for m in own if (m[\"registry\"], m[\"id\"]) in keys]\r\n        )\r\n    return own or []\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _commit_bases(root, base, head):\r\n    \"\"\"The trees the commit being judged is compared with: `base`, and, for\r\n    the index against HEAD while a merge is in progress, MERGE_HEAD too.\"\"\"\r\n    if head is not None or base != \"HEAD\":\r\n        return [base]\r\n    merging = (_git(root, [\"rev-parse\", \"-q\", \"--verify\", \"MERGE_HEAD\"]) or \"\").strip()\r\n    return [\"HEAD\"] + ([merging] if merging else [])\r\n\r\n\r\ndef marked_refusal(root, base, head, dial, paths=None):\r\n    \"\"\"THE NARROWED MARKER ARM: the refusal for a commit made under the loop\r\n    marker outside a claimed lane (the caller tests both) that moves a held\r\n    status or makes a held approval claim, or None. The tree `head` (None: the\r\n    index, judged against HEAD and MERGE_HEAD during a merge) is judged\r\n    against `base` under `dial`: every status move of the off-spine registries\r\n    and of the need, requirement, design and test tiers whose rung the dial\r\n    holds (`held_status_lines`), and every held copy claim (b) of\r\n    `held_claims`, with no exception; a live move into approval is already a\r\n    status move. `paths` narrows both to the registries a path-scoped commit\r\n    takes.\r\n\r\n    Implements: SR-208, LLR-246\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    bases = _commit_bases(root, base, head)\r\n    lines = held_status_lines(dial, _own_moves(root, bases, head, paths))\r\n    claims, _after, _befores, failures = _claims_against(root, bases, head, dial)\r\n    named = _named(paths)\r\n    for key, kind in sorted(claims.items()):\r\n        carriers = acceptance_record._tier_carriers(key[1], key[2])\r\n        if kind == \"b\" and (\r\n            named is None or any(c in named or _RECORD + c in named for c in carriers)\r\n        ):\r\n            lines.append(_claim_line(key, kind, dial))\r\n    lines += failures\r\n    if not lines:\r\n        return None\r\n    return (\r\n        \"the loop may not change a status or claim an approval the approval \"\r\n        \"level holds for a human (human_approval_through = {}): {} - a held \"\r\n        \"status moves only in a person's own reviewed commit, and a held \"\r\n        \"approval lands from a lane only as a CLARITY re-attestation bound to \"\r\n        \"its judged text\".format(dial, \"; \".join(lines))\r\n    )\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
